/* M12 WP3 Phase 5 — the already-open indicator: what this workspace WOULD fire on its
   next open. A readout, not a control (no pointer affordance, no click target).

   ⚠️ `flex-shrink: 0` is deliberate and `.workspace-header-name` above is the reason.
   The name ellipsizes but declares no shrink limit, so a shrinkable sibling would let
   the browser squeeze THIS instead of the name — or, worse, resolve the contest
   differently at different header widths. P3.9 was exactly this defect one surface
   over: a conditionally-rendered picker cell let the text stack absorb its width, so a
   37-char project name truncated while a LONGER 35-char name on the adjacent row did
   not. Keeping this rigid means the name is the only thing that ever gives. */
.workspace-header-nextopen {
  flex-shrink: 0;
  padding: 0.05rem 0.35rem;
  border-radius: 3px;
  background-color: rgba(110, 168, 255, 0.12);
  color: #6ea8ff;
  font-size: 0.72rem;
  white-space: nowrap;
}

/* M12 WP3 Phase 5 — the manual /session-start button. Deliberately ONE hardcoded
   button, not a registry: M13 builds the generic skill palette and either absorbs
   this or keeps it as a pinned special case.

   Styled as a quiet secondary action rather than a primary one — it is the 2.7% path
   (the log-mined share of cold opens that start a fresh workflow session), so it must
   be reachable without competing with the project name for attention. */
.workspace-session-start {
  flex-shrink: 0;
  padding: 0.1rem 0.4rem;
  border: 1px solid rgba(128, 128, 128, 0.35);
  border-radius: 3px;
  background-color: transparent;
  color: inherit;
  opacity: 0.7;
  font-family: inherit;
  font-size: 0.72rem;
  cursor: pointer;
}

.workspace-session-start:hover {
  opacity: 1;
  border-color: rgba(110, 168, 255, 0.6);
}

